[center][b][size=5]🏗️ MAPI - Schedule One Modding API[/size][/b]
[i]A comprehensive building framework and modding API for Schedule One - create custom buildings, interiors, and game modifications[/i][/center]

[size=5][b]✨ What is MAPI?[/b][/size]

MAPI is a comprehensive building framework and modding API designed specifically for Schedule One. It provides a robust foundation for creating custom buildings, interiors, and game modifications with an easy-to-use, component-based architecture.

Perfect for modders who want to add custom structures and gameplay features without the hassle of asset bundles!

[size=5][b]🎯 Who Needs This?[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Players[/b]: Only if you're using mods that declare MAPI as a requirement
[*][b]Mod Developers[/b]: If you want a robust, component-based building framework and modding API for Schedule One
[/list]

[size=5][b]🚀 Key Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]🏠 Building System[/b]: Complete building framework with support for walls, furniture, lighting, and structural elements
[*][b]📦 Component Architecture[/b]: Modular component system for reusable building pieces and custom functionality
[*][b]🎨 Procedural Meshes[/b]: Generate custom meshes programmatically with support for primitives and advanced mesh operations
[*][b]📁 GLTF Importing[/b]: Built-in GLTF model loading and processing for importing custom 3D assets
[*][b]🔧 Extension Methods[/b]: Comprehensive extension methods for Unity components, transforms, materials, and more
[*][b]📋 Configuration System[/b]: Flexible configuration system with palette support for building presets
[*][b]🎯 Game Integration[/b]: Seamless integration with Schedule One's materials, meshes, and prefabs
[/list]

[size=5][b]📦 Installation[/b][/size]

[b]For Players:[/b]

If a mod you want to use requires MAPI:

[list=1]
[*]Download the MAPI zip from the Files section
[*]Extract the zip - it contains both [font=Courier New]MAPI-Mono.dll[/font] and [font=Courier New]MAPI-Il2Cpp.dll[/font]
[*]Copy the correct DLL for your Steam branch to your game's [font=Courier New]UserLibs[/font] folder:
[list]
[*][b]Regular Steam branch (default)[/b]: Use [font=Courier New]MAPI-Il2Cpp.dll[/font]
[*][b]Alternate Steam branch[/b]: Use [font=Courier New]MAPI-Mono.dll[/font]
[/list]
[*]Launch the game - MAPI will load automatically with MelonLoader
[/list]

[b]To check your Steam branch:[/b] Right-click Schedule One in Steam → Properties → Betas. If it shows "None" or no selection, you're on the regular branch (use Il2Cpp).

[b]For Mod Developers:[/b]

To use MAPI in your mod project:

[list=1]
[*]Add the [b]Mono[/b] MAPI DLL as a reference to your mod project (via NuGet or direct DLL reference)
[*]Build your mod against the Mono DLL - it will work on both runtimes
[*]Users will need to install MAPI separately as a dependency with the correct DLL for their Steam branch
[/list]

[size=5][b]🔨 Building from Source[/b][/size]

For developers who want to build from source:

[list=1]
[*]Clone the repository
[*]Copy [font=Courier New]local.build.props.example[/font] to [font=Courier New]local.build.props[/font]
[*]Edit [font=Courier New]local.build.props[/font] and set your game installation path
[*]Build with [font=Courier New]dotnet build -c Mono[/font] or [font=Courier New]dotnet build -c Il2cpp[/font]
[/list]

[size=5][b]⚙️ Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*].NET Framework 4.7.2+ or .NET 6.0+
[*]MelonLoader (for mod development)
[*]Schedule One game installation
[/list]

